   "notes": "Montagu House (Sidney Sussex), Sidney St front north of the Sussex St corner. 1930s neo-Georgian: rubbed red brick upper floors with stone dressings, stone-faced shop ground floor (Costa at the south corner, other units north), three floors of small-pane sashes, slate mansard with dormers. Photos look along the street so bay count (10) and shop divisions are estimated; vertical scale squeezed to LiDAR eave 11 m."
